libfprint-2-tod1-broadcom-installer (0.3.0~24.04.1) noble; urgency=medium

  * FINAL RELEASE. This package is no longer maintained. The driver is now
    packaged for 24.04 and 26.04, in a newer version (5.15.377), by the Canonical
    engineer who maintains it upstream: ppa:medicalwei/dell-cv3-cv3plus. Use that
    instead. This release exists to fix removal and to say so.
  * Removing the package now takes the driver back out reliably. Previously, if
    the installer had been run more than once, removal reported success while
    leaving the proprietary driver on the machine. Anyone affected gets the fix
    by upgrading to this version before removing.
  * Removal now leaves alone any driver this package did not install, so it
    cannot delete a driver you installed from somewhere else. It says plainly
    that nothing was removed, and no longer advises you to switch off a
    fingerprint login that is still working.
  * Removing the package no longer leaves the downloaded driver in the cache.
  * Broadcom's own download is used as a second source when Canonical's copy
    cannot be reached. Both are pinned to a checksum, and the installer says
    which one it used.
  * Re-running the installer repairs a partly-installed driver instead of
    reporting that there is nothing to do, and it no longer downloads anything
    when the driver is already fully in place.
  * The proprietary licence is installed alongside the driver.

 -- Daniel Iwugo <daniel@themalwarefiles.com>  Thu, 30 Jul 2026 14:00:00 +0100

libfprint-2-tod1-broadcom-installer (0.1.0~24.04.1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Initial release. Fetches the Broadcom BCM58200 ControlVault 3 fingerprint
    TOD driver from Canonical's archive, verifies it against a pinned SHA256,
    and installs it on Ubuntu releases newer than 22.04. The proprietary driver
    is never redistributed by this package. (LP: #2099655)

 -- Daniel Iwugo <daniel@themalwarefiles.com>  Sun, 31 May 2026 20:57:23 +0100
